ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/run-statements/gpu-checks-bundle.md:65:**Change (only this criterion; everything else unchanged).** For `attn.k.bias`, the relative-to-itself criterion is replaced by: 0 non-finite and max(max|Δ|, max|compiled|, max|eager|) ≤ **0.05 × max|eager grad of the same block's `attn.q.bias`|**. The CPU BF16 residue ratio is 5.8e-3, so the bound leaves about 9× headroom, while a corrupted, O(1) gradient would exceed it. `c2_trunk_bwd.py` now also records `max_abs_diff`, `ref_max_abs` and `out_max_abs` per parameter (sha256 `12b46fd7…`; the comparisons are unchanged). `driver.py` (`15b41c74…`) applies the amended rule. `launch.sh` (`32d69f31…`) uses `timeout -k 20 3540`, so the aggregate driver wall stays ≤ 60 min (attempt 1 used 55.4 s). The internal deadline stays 55 min. Other scripts are unchanged.
