ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md:320:  - **Outer-timeout cleanup (post-run fix).** Both recorded attempts ran a driver that started each stage in its own session with no signal handler, so launch.sh's outer `timeout` could not have terminated running stages. Neither attempt came near that timeout, and attempt 1's ordinary stop terminated its running stage. The driver and launcher were revised after the run: SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP and exit handlers terminate every stage group, and `timeout -s TERM` signals the driver first. A local dummy-stage test passed (`gpu-checks-2026-09-29/post-run/driver_cleanup_test_local.txt`). The fix has not run on the pod.
